{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7ESmnLFyQoio5KqXF5L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written it to sound as confident as your numbers allow. Each claim is something you can stand behind if a backer checks it.\n\n<final_document>\n# [Game Title]\n### A cooperative board game for 1–4 players. One lighthouse. One family. One winter.\n\nThe keeper's family has to make it to spring. Everyone at the table plays on the same side, and you win or lose together.\n\n## Tested, not guessed\n\nMost games on crowdfunding pages are promises. This one has already been played, and played a lot.\n\n- **140 playtest sessions** since 2023\n- **About 60 different players** at the table\n- **Two conventions**, where strangers sat down and played it cold\n- **An 8.1 average rating** from its first 23 ratings on BoardGameGeek, before a single copy has been printed\n- **1,240 people** signed up to hear the moment this campaign went live\n\nI'll be straight about those numbers. Twenty-three ratings isn't a verdict from the whole hobby. But it is 23 people who played an unpublished game by an unknown designer and rated it highly. It's also 1,240 people who asked to be told when they could buy it. For a first game, that's as close to proof as you can get before it's printed.\n\n## What's already done\n\nThe things that usually go wrong in a first campaign are already handled:\n\n- **The art is finished.**\n- **The rules are finished**, refined over 140 sessions.\n- **The factory quote is signed:** 1,500 copies for $17,400.\n\nYour pledge doesn't pay for a game to be designed. It pays for a finished game to be printed and sent to you.\n\n## Where your money goes\n\nAt our $28,000 goal (about 570 backers):\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Printing 1,500 copies | $17,400 |\n| Platform and payment fees (~10%) | ~$2,800 |\n| Shipping to backers (~$9 per copy) | ~$5,150 |\n| Remaining | ~$2,650 |\n\nThere are no mystery line items. The goal covers the real cost of making this game and getting it to your door.\n\n## Who's making it\n\nI'm Owen Hale. This is my first published game.\n\nBy day I'm a land surveyor. My job is to measure carefully and get things exactly right, because someone is going to rely on the result. I've treated this game the same way: test it, watch what happens, adjust, and test it again, 140 times so far.\n\nI still work full time. That's why the schedule below is one I can keep, not one that sounds good.\n\n## When you'll get it\n\n**Expected delivery: November 2027.**\n\nI won't promise anything earlier. If that date changes, I'll tell you as soon as I know.\n\n## Back it\n\n**$49, with US shipping included.**\n\nIf you like cooperative games, and the idea of a family keeping a light burning through a long winter appeals to you, this is the game. It has been built carefully and tested hard, and it's ready to print.\n\nHelp me get it to the factory.\n</final_document>\n\nSome things to fix or check before you publish:\n\n- **There's no description of how the game plays.** This is the biggest gap. You didn't have the details, so I didn't make any up. Before launch, add two or three sentences on what players actually do on a turn and what makes it tense. A single real quote from a playtester would also help a lot.\n- **Placeholders and assumptions:** I used [Game Title] because I don't know the name. I also assumed the \"main ratings site\" is BoardGameGeek, so correct that if it isn't.\n- **Shipping outside the US** isn't mentioned. You'll need an answer before launch, because backers outside the US will ask.\n- **The ~$2,650 left over** is just arithmetic. I didn't call it a buffer for tariffs or freight, because you haven't planned it as one. It's worth deciding whether it is.\n- **\"I'll tell you as soon as I know\"** is a promise. Keep it only if you mean it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":10169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1210},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"283bf2d1-d062-4b47-8d38-631f1da9ea0b","uuid":"d29147ce-a13a-4eef-81e5-dc34335dec7a","timestamp":"2026-11-16T20:24:46.167Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7ESmYwoSL3RTT9YeTeE"}
